one of the pillars in the game from  really early on was this notion of  owning the battlefield and a lot of that  came from this idea that Lincoln's a  Vietnam vet and he has special training  and skills and tactical knowledge that a  normal mobster wouldn't that really  gives him the edge when he's going up  against waves of mobsters and his  training allows him to overcome those  odds and we really tried to incorporate  that into game play and a number of  different ways one we support stalking  in the game so you know you can go  through and you can stalk you're gonna  means you put yourself in the right  position take down an enemy we support a  wide variety of weapons so everything  from classic machine gun all the way to  Vietnam era weapons our version of some  of the weapons that they were using over  in Vietnam handguns that you might  expect the mobster to use all the way to  a more military feeling stuff we can  also gains the ability to put on a flak  vest he gains grenades and other things  that the mob initially at least doesn't  have access to we have a robust cover  system you know it's a type of world  game but we tried to make sure that  there was cover available everywhere and  take cover behind cars you can take  cover behind me pretty much anything in  the environment that looks like it  should be cover and then the way we can  move through the environment he's a  little bit more nimble than mobsters  he's a little bit more effective at  moving through combat and then finally  he's got not just his arsenal of ranged  weapons but he also has his fists and  his knife and one of my favourite parts  of the game are those the brutal  takedowns that you can do on mobsters  you get them stunned or you catch them  by surprise and many times if you pull  one of those off it will have kind of a  ripple effect and the guys around will  it's done for a moment and that gives  you an opening to take down another vest  so we tried to give player number of  tools to make me feel like he really  does own the battlefield  you
 

